\description{
Opens the interactive jabotR field notebook in the user's default web
browser. The application is distributed with the package and works
locally without an internet connection.

The field notebook allows users to organize collection-event and
specimen data, export a standardized JABOT spreadsheet, and generate
a printable field notebook in PDF format.

With `merge = TRUE`, a field notebook PDF previously generated by
`jabot_fieldbook()` is detected and its collection events are loaded
back into the notebook. A new collection event is opened with the next
number of the collector's sequence, so that the next PDF generated is a
new, more complete version of the field notebook covering the whole
collection-number sequence.
}
\details{
The field notebook runs locally using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files
distributed with jabotR. It does not require Shiny or an internet
connection. Spreadsheet generation is performed locally in the browser.

Every field notebook PDF embeds a machine-readable copy of its data as
nearly transparent text behind the notebook content (invisible on screen
and on paper, and it never adds pages). This is what allows
`merge = TRUE` to rebuild the notebook from the PDF. Merging requires the suggested packages \pkg{pdftools} and
\pkg{jsonlite}. PDFs generated before this feature was introduced, or
printed with a method that discards text (e.g. "print as image"),
cannot be merged.

The previous collection events are loaded collapsed, marked as coming
from the previous notebook, and remain editable. They are included in
the new PDF, but the JABOT spreadsheet exported from the merged notebook
contains only the new collection events (and is named after their
collection-number range), so records already submitted to JABOT are not
duplicated.
}
